               command-line program to build the optional IRIS IOx application
               packages (iris-arm64.tar / iris-amd64.tar). It is NOT part of this
               source repository and is NOT redistributed here.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party programs installed in the distributed server image
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The IRIS iris-aead helper (tools/iris-aead.c, Apache-2.0) is statically linked
with OpenSSL 3.5.8 libcrypto (Apache-2.0) and musl libc 1.2.6 (MIT). It uses
OpenSSL's AES-256-SIV implementation; IRIS does not implement that primitive.
The source and build scripts are shipped in tools/build-instruction-crypto*.
OpenSSL's upstream LICENSE.txt and musl's COPYRIGHT are combined in
iris-aead.LICENCE: beside the helper in Guest Shell bundles and the server's
/opt/iris/bin, and under /usr/local/share/licenses in the IOx/XR image.
OpenSSL source: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/tree/openssl-3.5.8

Guest Shell bundles additionally carry a separate static OpenSSH portable
10.5p1 ssh-keygen for Ed25519 instruction verification on older device hosts.
It is built by tools/build-ssh-verifier.sh from pinned upstream source, using
musl libc 1.2.6 (MIT); no OpenSSL library is linked. The upstream OpenSSH
LICENCE and musl COPYRIGHT are included together as agent/ssh-keygen.LICENCE
in every bundle. musl's complete notice is also in tools/licenses/musl-COPYRIGHT
(https://musl.libc.org/releases/musl-1.2.6.tar.gz).

