installs the following Debian system packages. They are redistributed inside
that image as separate, unmodified programs; IRIS does not link against, embed,
or derive from any of them. Each remains under its own license. Licenses are
named as the upstream projects publish them; consult each project for the
authoritative text.

  * sshpass  — GNU General Public License, version 2 (GPLv2).
               Installed as a system package and invoked as a subprocess
               (argv ["sshpass", "-e", "scp", ...]) so the audit-export upload
               and the server-side device sessions can supply an SSH password
               from the environment. Never modified, never linked.

  * age      — MIT License. Copyright (c) The age Authors.
               Installed as a system package and invoked as a subprocess to
               encrypt and decrypt the at-rest secret store (IRIS_AGE_BIN).

  * OpenSSH client (ssh, scp)
             — BSD-style OpenSSH license, with components under other
               permissive terms. Copyright (c) 1995 Tatu Ylonen and the
               OpenSSH contributors. Installed as a system package and invoked
               as a subprocess for every server-side device session and for the
               audit-export upload.

  * curl     — curl license (MIT/X derivative). Copyright (c) 1996-2026
               Daniel Stenberg and contributors. Installed as a system package;
               invoked by the image's own HEALTHCHECK.

  * ca-certificates
             — Mozilla Public License 2.0 (the CA certificate data);
               the Debian packaging scripts are under their own terms.
               Installed as a system package to supply the system trust store.

  * unzip    — Info-ZIP license (BSD-style). Copyright (c) 1990-2009
               Info-ZIP. Installed as a system package; present for operator
               convenience inside the container.

  * iproute2 — GNU General Public License, version 2. Installed as a system
               package; present for operator diagnostics inside the container.

The common IOx and IOS-XR device image (device/container/Dockerfile) installs a
smaller set of the same kinds of packages under the same terms; see that file
for the exact list shared by both runtime profiles.

